Third-party services
--------------------
boat.dev provides the optional per-agent cloud VMs. Legion calls its public REST API with your own API key.
boat.dev is a separate service with its own terms. No boat.dev documentation or code is included here.

Blender components (downloaded on request, never bundled)
---------------------------------------------------------
Legion's optional Blender bridge downloads its parts only when you press Set up in Settings. None is in this
repository or its history.
- Blender Lab MCP server (official). GPL-3.0-or-later. Downloaded from its official source (a pinned release
  archive with a pinned sha256) into your Legion data folder. It stays a separate program that Legion talks to
  over stdio and a local socket. Legion's own code is not a derivative of it and remains MIT.
- Community Blender MCP add-on. MIT. Downloaded from its upstream address (trust on first use) and installed into
  your own Blender.
- Blender itself (GPL) is only downloaded inside your own cloud VM, if you choose the VM sandbox.
Get a proper licence check before you redistribute a build that includes any of these downloads.
See docs/BLENDER.md.

BSV knowledge pack (src/core/kg/seeds/bsv.json)
-----------------------------------------------
The optional BSV pack is Legion-written text that summarises public documentation, in our own words. Each note
lists its sources and what we recorded about their licence in its `sources` field. Material used includes
b-open-io/1sat-university (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/; attribution: the 1Sat
University authors, https://github.com/b-open-io/1sat-university; summarised and adapted), documentation and
code from the BSV Association and bsv-blockchain repositories (Open BSV License, a modified MIT whose grant is
limited to the BSV blockchain and its testnets) and BRC standards (bsv.brc.dev). Some sources had no licence we
could read; for those the pack states the fact in fresh words and copies no text. Legion includes no code from any
of these projects. Trademarks belong to their owners.

